Source: andaru
Section: net
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Andaru project <apt@andaru.io>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13), gpg
Standards-Version: 4.7.2
Rules-Requires-Root: no
Homepage: https://github.com/andaru-project/andaru
Vcs-Browser: https://github.com/andaru-project/andaru
Vcs-Git: https://github.com/andaru-project/andaru.git

Package: andaru
Architecture: any
Depends: iproute2, nftables, systemd (>= 257), ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: apparmor, kea-dhcp4-server, kea-dhcp6-server, openssh-server, unbound
Description: firewall and router for Debian
 Andaru turns a Debian host into a firewall and router: interfaces, VLANs,
 bridges, addresses and routes through systemd-networkd, filtering and NAT
 through nftables, DHCP through Kea and DNS through Unbound, all from one
 validated configuration that is applied with a confirmation and rolled back
 when the administrator loses access.

Package: andaru-archive-keyring
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}
Multi-Arch: foreign
Description: OpenPGP key and APT source of the Andaru archive
 The key that signs https://apt.andaru.io/ and the APT source that trusts it
 for that repository only. Installing it lets APT install and upgrade Andaru.
